.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH cog-changelog 1  "cog-changelog " 
.SH "نام (NAME)"
cog\-changelog \- Display a changelog for the given commit oid range
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBcog\-changelog\fR [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-at\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-template\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-owner\fR] [\fB\-\-repository\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-unified\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATTERN\fR] 
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Display a changelog for the given commit oid range
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-at\fR \fI<AT>\fR
Generate the changelog for a specific git tag
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
Generate the changelog with the given template.

Possible values are \*(Aqremote\*(Aq, \*(Aqfull_hash\*(Aq, \*(Aqdefault\*(Aq or the path to your template. If not specified cog will use cog.toml template config or fallback to \*(Aqdefault\*(Aq.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR
Url to use during template generation
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-owner\fR \fI<OWNER>\fR
Repository owner to use during template generation
.TP
\fB\-\-repository\fR \fI<REPOSITORY>\fR
Name of the repository used during template generation
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-unified\fR
Combine package and global changes into one changelog
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATTERN\fR]
Generate the changelog in the given spec range
